-- `output_path_collision` (backend.md §2, *The output tree does not depend
-- on the file system's case sensitivity*): the platform's sibling for `Prog`
-- is copied to `_platform/Prog.foreign.mjs` and its runtime, `js/PROG.js`,
-- to `_platform/PROG.foreign.mjs`. Those are two files on Linux and ONE on
-- macOS and Windows, where the second write wins — so the build is refused
-- rather than written, naming both output paths and both sources.
--
-- The headline case of the rule — two modules `Json.Decode` and
-- `JSON.Decode` — cannot be a fixture: it needs two source files that are
-- themselves one file on a case-insensitive system, so the repository would
-- not survive a checkout on a Mac. The two sources here differ by more than
-- case, which is what makes the fixture portable while the OUTPUTS still
-- fold together.
import Prog exposing (Program)


main : Program
main =
    Prog.say "hello"
